<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's IRSA says Q4 net lower at $7 million.</title>
<headline>Argentina's IRSA says Q4 net lower at $7 million.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to June 30.</p>
<p>Q4 net $7.0 million vs $8.2 million</p>
<p>Revs $10.2 million vs n/a.</p>
<p>Year</p>
<p>GDR $1.87 vs $2.21</p>
<p>Revs $35.2 million vs $58.6 million.</p>
<p>NOTE - IRSA, one of Argentina's leading real estate companies, reported earlier on Tuesday that it posted a net gain of $21 million in fiscal 1996 compared with $20.6 million in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;While net sales were below last year's level mainly due to the Argentine recession, which affected the sale of (real estate) developments, this impact was partially offset by the strong performance of rental properties, with rental revenues up 66 percent for this fiscal year,&quot; IRSA said.</p>
<p>Full company name is IRSA Inversiones y Representaciones.</p>
<p>-- Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650</p>
</text>
